    "body": "Hi,\r\n\r\nSorry for the late response, been busy and forgot this was still open.\r\nAniRena is being reworked on, and will introduce later a API that can be accessed to read out statistics.\r\nAniRena is a partly closed tracker, but anonymous people can upload torrents.\r\nOnly torrents uploaded to AniRena, will be working on the back-end tracker, but any torrent that is not registered there, will not be accepted through the back-end tracker software.\r\n\r\n> Then, does AniRena add magnet support directly without uploading torrent files? If so, I hope to inform me how to use it.\r\n\r\nMagnet links are generated based on the torrent that is uploaded. Torrents got the SHA1 hashes needed in order to do anything at all. If a torrent is not uploaded to AniRena, it's not registered, and will not be handled by the back-end tracker.\r\n\r\n> Finally, can I collect AniRena for animeTackerList? I will add it to the readme.\r\n\r\nYou can collect torrents from AniRena, no problem, it's made for that. New site will even make it easier for third party applications to communicate with AniRena.\r\n\r\nI am also hosting a pure public back-end tracker, called gbitt.info which is a side project next to AniRena, which does accept any torrent.\r\n\r\nHope this is informative enough.\r\n\r\nKind regards.\r\nPower2All",
